//File:    LOCKED.jtext
//Date:    2026-11-17
//Purpose: A source file locked in for ONE OS: RHEL 9. Do not edit contract26.cc; to move it to a
//         new GCC release, replace it with that release's file and update the rows below.
//
// Why: GCC 16 links -lstdc++exp whenever -fcontracts is on the link line (the default
// contract-violation handler lives there). RHEL 9's gcc-toolset-16 does not ship libstdc++exp.a:
// its gcc.spec (CentOS Stream dist-git, gcc-toolset-16-gcc, branch c9s, commit e3206d72) moves only
// libstdc++.*a and libstdc++fs.*a into the toolset and then runs
//     rm -f %{buildroot}%{_prefix}/%{_lib}/{libffi*,libiberty.a,libstdc++*,libgfortran*}
// so every v002 gcc16 link on RHEL 9 failed with "cannot find -lstdc++exp" (RHEL-09-001,
// 2026-11-17). gcc-toolset-15 on RHEL 9 drops it the same way.
//
// What: contract26.cc is the only member of libstdc++exp.a that -fcontracts needs (the default
// handler: __handle_contract_violation, handle_contract_violation,
// std::contracts::invoke_default_contract_violation_handler). The stacktrace / print /
// filesystem members are not used by -fcontracts and are not copied.
//
// How: stdcxx_exp.cmake builds it with THIS machine's gcc-toolset-16 into
// <build>/stdcxx_exp/libstdc++exp.a, only when /etc/os-release is RHEL 9 AND the compiler is GCC 16
// AND that compiler has no libstdc++exp.a of its own. Every other OS: nothing is built or used.
//
